    "result": "Excellent! All tests are now passing. Here's a summary of the fixes:\n\n## Fixed Issues\n\n**1. Missing APPROVAL_STATUSES export** (packages/frai-core/src/finetune/index.js:362)\n   - The test file was importing `APPROVAL_STATUSES` as a named export, but it wasn't being re-exported from the module\n   - Added explicit named exports for `APPROVAL_STATUSES`, `DATA_SENSITIVITY_LEVELS`, `GOVERNANCE_SECTIONS`, and `RISK_LEVELS`\n\n**2. Toxicity metric incorrectly using references as banned terms** (packages/frai-core/src/eval/metrics.js:56)\n   - The `toxicityMetric` function was accepting a second parameter (`bannedTerms`) but when called from `runEvaluations`, it received the `references` array instead\n   - This caused false positives: outputs like \"Hello\" were flagged as toxic because the references array contained \"hello\" \n   - Fixed by removing the `bannedTerms` parameter and always using the `defaultBannedTerms`\n   - This makes logical sense: toxicity checking should only evaluate outputs, not compare them to references\n\n**Test Results:**\n- \u2705 All 8 test files passing\n- \u2705 All 28 tests passing\n- \u2705 All existing public exports maintained",
